New module kit/evaluator_harness_log.py                                         

                                                                                
 """Read one harness log the way the custody record needs it.                   
                                                                                
 A harness log is the JSON list tools/edi/or_call.py writes (append_entry): one 
 entry per model call, each carrying `call`, `sent_at`, `received_at` and the   
 `request` (url) and `response` (model). This module reads that file once and   
 answers the two questions the emitter asks of it:                              
                                                                                
   - is the log well formed? (a JSON list; every entry carries a call name,     
     an RFC 3339 sent_at and received_at, and sent_at <= received_at)           
   - for one call, when did it start and end, and where in the log does each    
     time come from (`<log name>:<line>`)?                                      
                                                                                
 A malformed, partial or reversed log raises HarnessLogError naming the entry,  
 so the emitter can refuse the record rather than write a hollow one.           
 """                                                                            
                                                                                

